  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef heard that four-leaf clovers bring good luck, so he went looking for one.\n\nIn his search, Chef found NNN clovers in total. Out of them, **exactly one** was a four-leaf clover, and all the others were three-leaf clovers.\n\nHow many leaves did Chef collect in total, across all the clovers?\n\n\nInput Format\nThe only line of input will contain a single integer NNN, the number of clovers Chef found.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint one integer: the total number of leaves Chef collected.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤101 \\leq N \\leq 101≤N≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5",
        "output": "16",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef found 555 clovers. One of them is a four-leaf clover, and the other four are three-leaf clovers.\nSo, the total number of leaves is 4+3⋅4=4+12=164 + 3\\cdot 4 = 4 + 12 = 164+3⋅4=4+12=16."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1",
        "output": "4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef found only one clover. It has to be a four-leaf clover, so Chef collected 444 leaves in total."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "10",
        "output": "31",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef found 101010 clovers. One of them is a four-leaf clover, and the others are three-leaf clovers.\nSo, the total number of leaves is 4+3⋅9=4+27=314 + 3\\cdot 9 = 4 + 27 = 314+3⋅9=4+27=31."
      }
    ]
  },
